[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551425646","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2551425646","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2551425646,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YE6pu","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T14:12:11Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T14:12:11Z","body":"I'm not 100% sure we want this, but if we do want this I think we should remove the non-const `ptr()` here.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551425646/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551448399","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2551448399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2551448399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YFANP","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T14:22:01Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T14:22:01Z","body":"> if we do want this I think we should remove the non-const `ptr()` here.\r\n\r\nI agree; I had started with the implementation of that but since it was a few hundred lines of changes I thought it may be better to introduce it softly first. But I would also be onboard with a hard-switch.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551448399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551456791","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2551456791","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2551456791,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YFCQX","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T14:25:31Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T14:25:31Z","body":"I'm not sure about this one either. Why have `ptrw()` at all if there's no CoW with `LocalVector`? Just so that you can switch back and forth between `LocalVector` and `Vector` without needing to update existing code with `ptrw()`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551456791/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551473489","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2551473489","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2551473489,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YFGVR","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T14:32:46Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T14:33:41Z","body":"> I'm not sure about this one either. Why have `ptrw()` at all if there's no CoW with `LocalVector`? Just so that you can switch back and forth between `LocalVector` and `Vector` without needing to update existing code with `ptrw()`?\r\n\r\nYes, that's one reason.\r\n\r\nAnother is that the existence of the `ptrw` API on the `CowData` end implies that a `ptr` call yields a const pointer, which is a bit confusing, and could lead to misinterpretation.\r\n\r\nFinally, I was running into a bit of trouble with the absence of a dedicated `const pointer` producing function with Spans (#100293). A `Span(ptr(), size())` call produces a mutable span (`Span<int>`) for `LocalVector`, which is unfortunately incompatible with parameters of type `Span<const int>` - so producers need an explicit const cast, leading to unnecessary boilerplate. With `Vector` and `String`'s APIs, you can use `Span(ptr(), size())` vs `Span(ptrw(), size())`.\r\n\r\nThe last point is somewhat of a \"future problem\" but since I already ran into it with local tests, I wanted to go ahead and try to pre-address since the earlier points are reason enough (for me) to have it merged.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551473489/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2552588210","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2552588210","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2552588210,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YJWey","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-19T01:31:25Z","updated_at":"2024-12-19T01:31:25Z","body":"I'm onboard with a hard-switch in theory. There's no real need to stagger this concept out across multiple PRs, and the change is compact enough to be unlikely to cause merge conflicts. In practice though, making sweeping changes to add a misnomer is... Odd\r\n\r\nThe API of `ptrw` is arguably flawed to begin with; most other identical-minus-const functions follow the convention already used in `LocalVector` of just sharing names (ex: all `operator[]` functions). I'm not saying that would warrant changing all existing instances of `ptrw` to `ptr`, but it feels *more* appropriate if the endgoal was API unification\r\n\r\nI'm certainly not dying on that hill though. Hard-swapping to `ptrw` ultimately makes the most sense","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2552588210/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2555760555","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2555760555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2555760555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YVc-r","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-19T20:57:22Z","updated_at":"2024-12-19T20:57:22Z","body":"The whole point of this is to make it easier to swap between containers when a place is found to improve performance.\r\n\r\nTo facilitate this we do need to make sure that you can actually do this, so that means that ptrw() and ptr() should work same on LocalVector\r\n\r\nIf it doesn't work the same, and just exists, then it's really not fit for purpose and we shouldn't bother imho.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2555760555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2555769091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2555769091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2555769091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YVfED","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-19T21:02:49Z","updated_at":"2024-12-19T21:02:49Z","body":"> The whole point of this is to make it easier to swap between containers when a place is found to improve performance.\r\n> \r\n> To facilitate this we do need to make sure that you can actually do this, so that means that ptrw() and ptr() should work same on LocalVector\r\n> \r\n> If it doesn't work the same, and just exists, then it's really not fit for purpose and we shouldn't bother imho.\r\n\r\nAlright, I think I feel the same way. I'll adjust the PR to actually switch uses of mutable `ptr()` to `ptrw()`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2555769091/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558435358","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2558435358","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2558435358,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YfqAe","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-22T12:13:36Z","updated_at":"2024-12-22T12:17:33Z","body":"Alright, I performed the replacement. It's just about 120 LOC, so nothing too crazy. I still think it's absolutely worth it to reduce the overhead of having to remember whether you're dealing with a `Vector` or `LocalVector` right now.\r\n\r\nWhile doing this I was wondering whether it wouldn't be more appropriate to rename the `ptrw` functions to `ptr` (as overloads) for `Vector` and `CowData`. But I don't think it's possible to nudge the compiler to use the const overload for non-const objects, since C++ doesn't have backwards type inference. And it may also be awkward having to explain people to remember using the `const` keyword on their variables to avoid an accidental fork. So I guess this `w` suffix is required.\r\n\r\nEdit: This may take a few attempts because of platform-specific uses I cannot test locally...","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558435358/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2562097775","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2562097775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2562097775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YtoJv","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T02:47:23Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T02:47:23Z","body":"> The whole point of this is to make it easier to swap between containers when a place is found to improve performance.\r\n\r\nOh yes please. Switching all the time between `Vector.ptrw()` and `LocalVector.ptr()` when bouncing between two versions is so extra annoying atm. In the last PR dev alone with all those pathfinding arrays I had to switch it like 100+ times mostly manually. At some point I really started to dread it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2562097775/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2582992320","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2582992320","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2582992320,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z9VXA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T15:42:34Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T15:51:16Z","body":"I don't think this is a good idea, fundamentally I think there should never be duplicate methods in any API, it adds confusion and pitfalls. `Vector` and `LocalVector` already have unique quirks to handle switching between the two which are far greater than `ptr/ptrw` like `write`, so I don't think the argument of easing moving from `Vector` to `LocalVector`\r\n\r\n> I'm definitely in favor of this change. ptrw is more consistent and makes any writes instantly visible in the code.\r\n\r\nI'd argue this is just as obvious from context, like `memcpy(foo.ptr(), ...)` is obvious from the place, or `T *p = foo.ptr()` is obvious from typing that it is a mutable pointer","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2582992320/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583025760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2583025760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2583025760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z9dhg","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T15:52:07Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T15:56:14Z","body":"> I don't think this is a good idea, fundamentally I think there should never be duplicate methods in any API, it adds confusion and pitfalls. `Vector` and `LocalVector` already have unique quirks to handle switching between the two which are far greater than `ptr/ptrw` like `write`, so I don't think the argument of easing moving from `Vector` to `LocalVector`\r\n\r\nThis is only slightly on topic, but: \r\nI often view duplicate methods in APIs as _positive_, specifically when both names convey _different intent_. The idea behind that is encapsulation: Just because the functions _happen to_ do the same things on the inside, the intent when calling them may be different, and it helps readers and maintainers understand better what is happening on the caller's side.\r\nThis kind of thing may actually happen a lot if you try to work towards consistency between APIs, as implementations of one concept _may happen to_ require the same implementation as another for one specific implementer.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583025760/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583040627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2583040627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2583040627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z9hJz","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T15:56:04Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T15:57:37Z","body":"I'd say that has to be balanced against the communication of effect and function, and there are other ways of communicating intent that are just as clear IMO, without the cost of confusion for users picking methods\r\n\r\nI'd say consistency is about *function* more than intent, an API *communicates* to the user what the class does\r\n\r\nI'd say that in *most* cases the use of `ptrw` would be conveyed by context already, the exception being calling unknown methods with the pointer, like `foo(bar.ptr())` and not being able to tell if `foo` takes `T *` or `const T *`, but most of the time you have things like well known methods like `memcpy` or explicit from `T *p = foo.ptr()`\r\n\r\nI personally think adding duplicate methods hurts readability and usability and our containers are already a bit esoteric and hard to quite figure out at times, and I'd argue the distinction between `ptr/ptrw` is *specifically* because of the COW nature of those types, and helps convey *mutation* of those types, i.e. what the method triggers","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583040627/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583060288","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2583060288","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2583060288,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z9l9A","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T16:00:25Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T16:00:25Z","body":"> I'd argue the distinction between `ptr/ptrw` is _specifically_ because of the COW nature of those types, and helps convey _mutation_ of those types, i.e. what the method triggers\r\n\r\nThis is definitely a valid concern! I think it's similar to what @clayjohn was saying in the Rocket Chat discussion about this change.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583060288/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583094259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100555#issuecomment-2583094259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100555","id":2583094259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z9uPz","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T16:07:48Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T16:16:51Z","body":"As a tangent I'd say the *opposite* would be interesting to have in general for our container, an equivalent to the `begin/cbegin` of the STL, having the ability to access explicitly a `const` pointer, though with `Vector` this would become a bit redundant as it has `ptr/ptrw`\r\n\r\nBut it *would* give us an option of a threefold system:\r\n* `ptrc` or `ptrr` (i.e. a `ptr_read` against `ptr_write`) or `cptr` for read-only access (`const` and doesn't mutate)\r\n* `ptr` for read/write access (non-`const` and doesn't mutate)\r\n* `ptrw` for read/write mutating access","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583094259/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]